# 🚗 NYC Collisions Dashboard

An interactive Power BI dashboard analyzing vehicle collisions across New York City to uncover safety insights and trends.


## 📊 Project Overview
This project visualizes NYC motor vehicle collision data to identify high-risk areas, patterns over time, and contributing factors.  
It aims to support urban safety planning and improve awareness around road incidents.


## 🧠 Key Insights
-Brooklyn and Queens remain the city’s most accident-prone areas.
-Friday evenings show the highest collision and injury rates.
-Driver inattention is the leading contributing factor across years.
-There was a temporary dip in 2024 followed by a rise in 2025, indicating fluctuating urban driving behaviors or enforcement effectiveness.


## 🧰 Tools & Skills
- SQL – Data extraction and preprocessing from raw collision datasets
- Snowflake – Cloud-based data storage, querying, and modeling
- Power BI – Interactive dashboard design and visualization
- DAX – Custom measures for KPIs, severity scoring, and time intelligence


## 📈 Dashboard Highlights
- Visualized 2023–2025 collision patterns, showing a sharp dip in 2024 followed by a rebound in 2025.
- Mapped collision hotspots across boroughs, with Brooklyn and Queens recording the highest incidents.
- Identified top causes such as driver inattention, unsafe speed, and failure to yield.
- Highlighted peak severity during evening hours (7–10 PM) and highest collisions on Fridays.

